# Chroma library, modern Earth: ECHOES across stages (moments that come only from the person's own history). Plan: earth-plan.md "Across stages".
# Syntax: header of build.py. Each echo is even on its own: alpha even, the five one-color options and one full cross cycle (s1 to s4 in turn).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- marks: a word kept or broken, help given or refused

== a promise you broke comes back
tier: echo
stages: juvenile+
age: 13-110
stakes: .8
tone: trouble
life: friends, family, work
horizon: months
roles: friend, sibling, colleague
earth: someone you once let down brings up the old promise, just when you need their trust
after: mark 'broke your word', and the person it was given to (or someone who heard of it) now has a say in something the person needs
delay: 1-20
likelier: a small circle where people talk; a big or public promise; the person let down is still close
rarer: the person let down moved away or died; a small promise; the person owned up at the time
times: Common: perhaps 1 in 3 people who break a real promise later hear it raised when they need that person's trust (estimate)
scene: Over coffee, {friend} says it lightly: the last time {N} promised something, {friend} waited a whole summer for nothing.
scene W: {N} remembers giving {Ns} word to {friend}, and remembers the exact day it was broken. It has sat there ever since like an unpaid bill.
scene U: {N} goes back over it: what was promised, what changed, and why {friend} still brings it up after all these years.
scene B: {N} needs {friend} on side now, and {friend} has a long memory and every reason to say no.
scene R: The old promise comes back like a slap, and {Ns} face goes hot before {friend} has finished the sentence.
scene G: Some things do not stay buried. {friend} has carried that broken promise the way a tree carries an old cut in its bark.
- W | keep the old promise now, late as it is, whatever it costs | binds | v: benevolence, conformity | mark: kept your word | chance: 85
- U | explain what changed back then, and ask what would set it right | v: self-direction, benevolence | chance: 69
- B | point out the favours they never repaid, so the score is even | v: power | mark: made an enemy | chance: 49
- R | say sorry from the gut, there and then, and mean every word | v: benevolence | mark: owned up | chance: 88
- G | let them keep their grudge; some cuts take years to close | v: tradition (accepting what is) | chance: 50
- W>U | write down every promise you make from now on, and check the list weekly | habit | v: conformity, self-direction | chance: 62
- U>B | find out what they want now, and offer that instead of the old promise | v: power, achievement | chance: 72
- B>R | treat them to something fun, and laugh the whole thing off | v: hedonism | chance: 80
- R>G | turn up at their door with your sleeves rolled up, the way old friends do | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 85
- G>W | ask an elder you both trust to help settle it between you | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 78
works: {friend} hears it out, and the old promise stops standing between them.
works: The matter is settled, and {friend} says yes to what {N} needs.
fails: {friend} says no, and tells the old story to anyone who will listen.
fails: The talk goes badly, and an old hurt becomes a fresh one.

== a promise kept for years pays off
tier: echo
stages: young_adult+
age: 18-110
tone: joy
life: work, friends, community
horizon: months
roles: an old employer, friend, elder
earth: someone you never let down, years ago, now vouches for you or opens a door
after: mark 'kept your word' in a long or costly matter, or at least three times with the same person or group, and that person or group can now repay it
delay: 3-25
likelier: a small trade or town where reputations last; the same people over years
rarer: frequent moves; the one who remembers has died or retired
times: Perhaps 1 in 4 people who keep their word to one boss or group for years later get a door opened by them; (estimate; Granovetter found over half of jobs came through contacts)
scene: A letter comes from someone {N} worked for years ago. They remember that {N} kept every promise, and they have something to offer.
scene W: {N} kept that promise when it would have been easy not to. Now someone remembers, and says so in front of everyone.
scene U: {N} turns the offer over. Years of small kept promises, and here at last is what they add up to.
scene B: Years of keeping {Ns} word have built something {N} never counted: credit. Now it can be spent.
scene R: {N} had almost forgotten. Now someone is shaking {Ns} hand and saying they never did.
scene G: Seeds planted long ago come up in their own time. A phone call brings {N} the harvest of a promise kept.
- W | accept, and promise them the same care you gave before | v: conformity, benevolence | mark: kept your word | chance: 93
- U | read the small print and ask to see the books first | v: security, self-direction | chance: 72
- B | name your price; good faith has a market value | identity | v: power, achievement | chance: 80
- R | say yes on the spot and celebrate with whoever is near | v: stimulation, hedonism | chance: 90
- G | take it calmly, as the fruit of years of plain dealing | v: tradition | chance: 92
- W>B | take the post and climb it rung by rung, by the book | v: achievement, conformity | chance: 80
- U>R | negotiate a deal that leaves the summers free for travel | v: self-direction, stimulation | chance: 60
- B>G | use the opening to get someone in your family taken on as well | v: benevolence (family), power | chance: 78
- R>W | throw yourself into it, heart and soul, to repay their faith | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 90
- G>U | take it slowly, learning the ropes from the old hands | v: self-direction, tradition | mark: learned a skill | chance: 85
works: The new door opens wide, and {N} walks through it.
works: The trust holds, and the offer is every bit as good as it sounded.
fails: The offer turns out smaller than it sounded.
fails: Someone with louder friends gets it in the end.

== someone you helped returns the favour
tier: echo
stages: juvenile+
age: 18-110
tone: joy
life: any
horizon: week
roles: the one once helped, neighbour
earth: when you are in a fix, someone you once helped turns up and insists on helping
after: mark 'helped someone in need', and now the person is in need themselves and the one once helped can help
delay: 2-30
likelier: a small town or close trade; the help was big; the person is in real trouble now
rarer: a big anonymous city; the help was small or given anonymously
times: Fairly common: perhaps 1 in 3 people who helped someone through a hard time are later helped back by them (estimate)
scene: {N} is moving house alone when a van pulls up. Out climbs someone {N} helped through a bad winter years ago, with two friends and a stack of boxes.
scene W: {N} helped because it was right, and never thought anyone was keeping count. Yet here they are, sleeves rolled up.
scene U: {N} watches them carry boxes and wonders how they even heard. Who told them {N} needed help?
scene B: A favour {N} did years ago and half forgot is being repaid, with interest.
scene R: {N} recognises the face at the door and laughs out loud, then nearly cries.
scene G: What goes around comes around. {N} gave when it was needed, and now it comes back, the way rain returns to the hills.
- W | accept graciously, and thank them properly in front of everyone | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 95
- U | ask how their life turned out since then, and really listen | v: self-direction, benevolence | mark: made a friend | chance: 90
- B | accept, and ask whether they could help with something bigger too | v: power, achievement | chance: 72
- R | hug them on the doorstep and open a bottle that night | v: hedonism, benevolence | chance: 93
- G | let them help and say nothing of debts; that is how it goes between people | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 93
- W>R | insist on cooking them a proper dinner, then let the evening run late | v: hedonism, benevolence | chance: 90
- U>G | write down their story, so the family remembers who helped whom | v: tradition | chance: 82
- B>W | use the goodwill to get them onto the street's helping rota | v: benevolence, power | chance: 82
- R>U | go along on a whim to see the project they run now | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 90
- G>B | keep them close; a loyal friend is worth more than money in the bank | v: security, power | chance: 85
works: The help comes just in time, and the day ends in laughter.
works: An old kindness turns into a new friendship.
fails: The help is kindly meant, but it tangles things more than it eases them.
fails: They come once, and then life pulls them away again.

== the one you turned away is the one who can help
tier: echo
stages: juvenile+
age: 18-110
stakes: .8
tone: trouble
life: any
horizon: week
roles: the one once refused, sibling
earth: you need help, and the one person who can give it is someone you once turned away
after: mark 'refused someone in need', and now the person is in need themselves and the one refused is the one who could help
delay: 2-30
likelier: a small town; the one refused has done well since; real trouble now
rarer: a big city with many other helpers; the refusal was small and long ago
times: Uncommon: perhaps 1 in 10 people who turned someone away later need that same person, mostly in small towns (estimate)
scene: The only one in town with a truck, the know-how and a free weekend is the neighbour {N} once shut the door on.
scene W: {N} remembers the night they knocked and {N} said no. Fair is fair, and {N} has no right to ask now.
scene U: {N} runs through the options again. There is only one person who can help, and {N} knows exactly why they might refuse.
scene B: {N} needs something from someone who owes {N} nothing, and who might enjoy saying no.
scene R: {Ns} stomach turns at the thought of knocking on that door. Pride and need pull in opposite directions.
scene G: The wheel has turned. This time {N} is the one at the door.
- W | do without; having refused them, you have no right to ask | v: conformity, universalism | chance: 40
- U | find some other way, however long it takes, rather than ask | identity | v: self-direction, security | chance: 62
- B | offer to pay well for the help, so nobody owes anybody | identity | v: power, security | chance: 80
- R | knock on their door and blurt out the whole story, pride and all | v: none clear (need spoken straight out) | chance: 80
- G | send a relative or friend they always liked to ask on your behalf | v: security, tradition | chance: 75
- W>G | apologise formally first, then ask, so the old wound can close | v: benevolence, conformity | mark: owned up | chance: 82
- U>W | work out what would be a fair return, and offer it with the request | v: universalism (fairness) | chance: 72
- B>U | pay for a course and learn to do it without anyone's help | v: self-direction, achievement | mark: learned a skill | chance: 71
- R>B | go anyway, and charm them until they cannot say no | v: power | chance: 70
- G>R | trust your gut about the right moment, then ask straight out | v: self-direction | chance: 72
works: The door opens, and the help comes without a word about the past.
works: {N} gets what is needed, and the old refusal is finally talked through.
fails: The answer is a flat no, and the whole street hears why.
fails: Help comes, grudgingly, with the old story attached.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- marks: enemies, friends, defiance

== an old enemy holds the keys
tier: echo
stages: young_adult+
age: 18-110
stakes: .9
tone: trouble
life: work, public life
horizon: months
roles: rival, boss
earth: the person you fell out with years ago now sits on the panel, runs the office or owns the building
after: mark 'made an enemy', and that enemy now holds a position over the person: a boss, an official, a landlord, a judge of something the person wants
delay: 3-30
likelier: a small trade or town; an ambitious enemy; the person stayed in the same field
rarer: a big world; a small quarrel; the enemy moved on or mellowed
times: Uncommon: perhaps 1 in 10 people who make an enemy later find that person their boss, landlord or judge, mostly in small fields (estimate)
scene: The new head of department walks in, and {N} knows the face at once: {rival}, from all those years ago.
scene W: {N} has always believed the rules protect everyone, even from old grudges. Now {N} will find out whether they do.
scene U: {N} studies {rival} across the table: what they want, what they remember, how much they have changed.
scene B: {rival} holds the keys now. {N} knows that feeling from the other side, and does not like it from this one.
scene R: Seeing {rival} in that chair makes {Ns} fists clench under the table.
scene G: Old enmities grow roots. {rival} has waited a long time, and now the season is theirs.
- W | go through the proper channels and ask for someone neutral to handle your case | v: security, conformity | chance: 67
- U | keep a careful record of every exchange, in case it comes to that | habit | v: security | chance: 60
- B | find out what they need now, and make yourself useful to them | v: power, security | chance: 82
- R | look them in the eye and say what everyone is thinking | v: self-direction | chance: 49
- G | keep your head down and wait; positions change, and so do people | v: security, tradition (patience) | chance: 67
- W>U | retrain properly, by the book, so your work speaks for itself | v: achievement | mark: learned a skill | chance: 78
- U>B | quietly gather what they would rather keep hidden, as insurance | v: power, security | closed: approval: prying into a boss's past; backfire: found out, and the feud goes public | chance: 48
- B>R | take a better offer elsewhere and enjoy telling them so | door | v: self-direction, hedonism | chance: 73
- R>G | rally your old friends around, so nobody stands alone against them | v: benevolence, security | chance: 75
- G>W | make peace the old way: a gift, a handshake, bygones left as bygones | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 70
works: {rival} turns out to have moved on, and treats {N} fairly.
works: The old feud is set aside, and the work goes on.
fails: {rival} finds a dozen small ways to make life hard.
fails: The old quarrel flares up again, in front of everyone.

== an old friend turns up when you need one
tier: echo
stages: young_adult+
age: 18-110
tone: joy
life: friends
horizon: week
roles: friend
earth: an old friend you lost touch with calls out of nowhere, just when things are hard
after: mark 'made a friend', a friendship that faded with distance or time, and now the person is in a hard stretch (a loss, an illness, a move, belonging low)
delay: 5-40
likelier: a hard stretch now; a reunion or a funeral that brings people together; easy contact by phone and internet
rarer: the friend has died; the friendship ended in a quarrel
times: Common: perhaps 1 in 3 people going through a hard stretch hear from a friend they had lost touch with; (estimate, easier since social media)
scene: The phone rings late in a bad week. It is {friend}, silent for years: "I just had a feeling. How are things, really?"
scene W: {friend} remembered {Ns} birthday every year, even after the letters stopped. Now {friend} is on the doorstep with a pot of soup.
scene U: {N} keeps wondering how {friend} knew. Somebody must have said something, or {friend} simply read between the lines.
scene B: {N} has spent years building a life that needs nobody. And yet here is {friend}, and {N} is glad.
scene R: {Ns} heart leaps at the voice on the phone. All the years apart vanish in a second.
scene G: Some friendships are like old paths, overgrown but still there under the leaves. {friend} has walked straight down one.
- W | set a day each month to call, so it never lapses again | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 79
- U | tell them honestly how bad things have been, and ask what they would do | v: self-direction, benevolence | chance: 88
- B | let them help, and keep your guard up about why they came back | v: security | chance: 80
- R | get on a train to see them that same weekend | v: stimulation, benevolence | body: light | chance: 92
- G | pick up exactly where you left off, as if no time had passed | v: tradition, benevolence | mark: made a friend | chance: 82
- W>B | accept their offer of a reference, and promise to live up to it | v: achievement, conformity | chance: 80
- U>R | plan the trip together that you always talked about back then | v: stimulation, hedonism | chance: 67
- B>G | use their contacts to get your family the help it needs right now | v: benevolence (family), power | chance: 82
- R>W | throw a party for the whole old crowd, so nobody drifts off again | v: benevolence, hedonism | chance: 82
- G>U | walk the old haunts together and talk over what the years have taught | v: self-direction, tradition | chance: 90
works: The friendship picks up as if it had never stopped.
works: {friend} stays close through the hard months, and things begin to lift.
fails: The call is warm, but the old ease does not come back.
fails: {friend} has troubles of their own, and the visit leaves them both tired.

== the office you defied remembers
tier: echo
stages: juvenile+
age: 14-110
tone: trouble
life: public life, work, school
horizon: months
roles: an official, a teacher, boss, elder
earth: the office, school or council you once stood up to has your name on file, and now you need something from it
