- U>W | write a clear, fair proposal that even the other side can accept | v: universalism, conformity | chance: 72
- B>U | use your new standing to get the papers they have been hiding | v: power, self-direction | chance: 48
- R>B | take the lead, and let everyone know whose fight this is now | v: power, achievement | chance: 78
- G>R | trust your instinct that it is someone else's turn, and enjoy the summer | v: hedonism, self-direction | mark: turned down a chance | chance: 58
works: People rally behind {N}, and the first meeting is packed.
works: The cause wins a small victory, and {Ns} name is said with respect.
fails: The meeting splits into arguments before anything is decided.
fails: The fight drags on, and {N} becomes its target.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- marks: pressure, a hidden wrong, a skill, a risk

== the same pressure, again
tier: echo
stages: juvenile+
age: 13-110
tone: trouble
life: friends, work, family
horizon: moment
roles: friend, colleague, boss, sibling
earth: the people who pushed you into something once are pushing again, and they expect the same answer
after: mark 'gave in to pressure', and the same kind of pressure comes again from the same people or the same sort of group
delay: 1-15
likelier: the same circle; giving in was rewarded last time; autonomy low now
rarer: a new circle; last time went badly and the person said so
times: Very common: most people who give in to a group once meet the same push from the same circle again, often within a year or two (estimate)
scene: The plan is the same as last time, and so is the pause before everyone at the table turns to look at {N}.
scene W: Last time {N} went along because everyone else did. The rules have not changed, and neither has the knot in {Ns} stomach.
scene U: {N} knows the pattern at once: the same people, the same pitch, the same silence before the question.
scene B: They pushed {N} once and it worked. They take {N} for an easy yes, which is worth knowing, and worth using.
scene R: {N} feels the old squeeze in the chest: wanting to belong, and hating to be told.
scene G: The current pulls the same way it pulled before. {N} can feel it tugging at {Ns} feet.
- W | report the ringleader to whoever is in charge | v: conformity, security | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: informing on the group; backfire: shut out by everyone | chance: 45
- U | ask for a day to think, and use it to look at the facts | v: self-direction | chance: 67
- B | go along again, but this time get something out of it | habit | v: power, achievement | mark: gave in to pressure | chance: 52
- R | snap that you are nobody's pushover, and walk out | v: self-direction | chance: 80
- G | go along; these are your people, for better or worse | v: conformity, security | mark: gave in to pressure | self_control: - | chance: 50
- W>U | make a firm rule in advance, and rehearse the word no | v: self-direction | chance: 82
- U>B | work out who is really behind the push, and deal with them alone | v: power | chance: 65
- B>R | promise to join, then quietly fail to turn up | v: hedonism, self-direction | mark: broke your word | chance: 65
- R>G | bring a loyal friend along, and stand firm together | v: security, benevolence | chance: 88
- G>W | ask the family what they think, and do as they say | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 72
works: The moment passes, and {N} feels lighter for it.
works: {N} comes out of it with friends intact and conscience clear.
fails: {N} ends up doing it again, and the old feeling comes back stronger.
fails: The group cools toward {N}, and the invitations thin out.

