- U>R | show them how to put it right quietly, so they are free of it | v: benevolence, self-direction | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: covering up a wrong; backfire: both found out | chance: 80
- B>G | cover for them, the way family covers for family | v: benevolence (in-group), security | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: covering up a wrong; backfire: both found out | chance: 72
- R>W | blurt out your own old wrong first, then report theirs | v: universalism (fairness), conformity | mark: owned up | chance: 78
