earth: at sixty, with the children grown, someone hands you a ticket to a place you have only seen on television
after: made not: no mark 'left home' or 'moved away' in the person's whole life, and travel passed up again and again (money, duty, fear); now duties have eased (children grown, retired) and a chance appears
delay: 20-60
likelier: duties eased; a little money; a child or friend who travels
rarer: poor health; no money; a partner who will not go
times: Perhaps 1 in 4 people who never travelled get a real chance once duties ease; about half of Americans hold a passport (US State Department)
scene: {child} slides an envelope across the kitchen table: two tickets, a passport form, and a map with a circle drawn on it.
scene W: {N} spent forty years keeping things running at home. There was always a reason to stay. Now the reasons have run out.
scene U: {N} has read about that city for decades, its streets and its history. Now the books could become a place.
scene B: {N} never spent money on going places. Now there is money, and time, and nobody left to spend it on but {N}.
scene R: The ticket shakes in {Ns} hand. All those years of postcards from other people's lives, and now one of {Ns} own.
scene G: {N} has lived a whole life in one valley. Leaving it, even for a fortnight, feels as strange as flying.
- W | go, with every day planned and the house left in order | v: security, conformity | chance: 85
- U | read everything about the place first, and keep a journal every day there | door | v: self-direction | chance: 82
- B | upgrade the tickets and do it in style; you have earned it | v: hedonism, power | chance: 92
- R | go, and leave the itinerary at home | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 85
- G | thank them, and say the valley is all the world you need | v: tradition, security | mark: turned down a chance | chance: 20
- W>U | join a proper group tour with a guide who knows the history | door | v: self-direction, security | chance: 88
- U>B | hunt down the bargain fares and stretch the trip to three countries | v: achievement, hedonism | chance: 62
- B>R | sell the old car to pay for a whole month away | v: stimulation, hedonism | chance: 88
- R>G | go and find the place your family came from, generations back | door | v: tradition, stimulation | chance: 82
- G>W | go only with the old friends from the club, so home comes along | v: security, tradition | chance: 79
works: {N} comes back with a suitcase of stories and a new look in the eye.
works: The trip goes beautifully, and the next one is planned before the bags are unpacked.
fails: The journey is exhausting, and {N} spends most of it longing for home.
fails: Something always comes up, and the tickets stay in the drawer.

== someone younger does what you always planned
