likelier: a long-held plan; a cautious life; a small field where news travels
rarer: the plan was dropped long ago; the person took other big chances
times: Fairly common: perhaps 1 in 4 cautious planners see someone younger do the very thing they long planned (estimate)
scene: There it is in the local paper: {colleague}, twenty-six, opening the very shop {N} has planned for fifteen years, on the very street.
scene W: {N} always said: when the children are grown, when the mortgage is paid, when it is the responsible time. That time never came.
scene U: {N} has three notebooks of plans, costings and sketches. {colleague} had none of them, and simply did it.
scene B: Someone else has taken the idea and run with it. {N} sat on it too long, and now it belongs to someone faster.
scene R: {N} reads the article twice and wants to scream. All that waiting, for nothing.
scene G: Every seed has its season. {N} kept this one in a drawer so long that it sprouted in someone else's soil.
- W | send them a card wishing them well, and mean it | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 88
- U | go to their opening and study what they got right and wrong | v: self-direction, achievement | chance: 62
