- R | quit your job that week and start anyway | identity | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 61
- G | let it go; some dreams are meant for other hands | v: tradition (accepting what is) | chance: 78
- W>B | report their shop to the inspectors for every rule it bends | v: power | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: reporting out of spite; backfire: known as the town busybody | chance: 15
- U>R | take the old notebooks and plan something wilder that nobody has done | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 55
- B>G | sell them your plans, and put the money toward the family | v: benevolence (family), power | chance: 58
- R>W | turn up on opening day and work the counter for nothing, to see it thrive | v: benevolence | mark: made a friend | chance: 88
- G>U | work a season in their shop, and learn what the planning never taught | door | v: self-direction, tradition | mark: learned a skill | chance: 67
works: {N} finds a way to make the old dream {Ns} own after all.
works: The sting fades, and {N} makes peace with the life that was chosen.
fails: Envy settles in, and {N} cannot walk down that street any more.
fails: {N} rushes in late, and the half-made plan costs dearly.

