scene U: {N} pulls out the spreadsheet from last time and starts comparing: what was cut, what worked, what hurt most.
scene B: After the last time, {N} swore never to be caught short again. And here it is.
scene R: The old panic is back in {Ns} chest, the same as when {N} was a child and the electricity was cut off.
scene G: Lean years come and fat years follow. {N} has lived through one winter like this, and knows how to bank the fire.
- W | bring back the strict budget from last time, line by line | habit | v: security, conformity | chance: 90
- U | study what went wrong last time, and cut where it hurts least | v: security, self-direction | chance: 82
- B | take cash work on the side, no questions asked | habit | v: security, power | closed: law: undeclared work; backfire: a tax bill and a fine | chance: 85
- R | spend a little on something joyful anyway; the lean years will not win | v: hedonism | chance: 80
- G | dig the garden over for vegetables, and lean on family | habit | v: security, tradition | body: light | chance: 82
